  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The charge on a condenser is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>V</mi></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>C</mi></mfrac><mi>Q</mi></math></p><p>Since the capacitance depends on the construction of the condenser, it is constant. Therefore, the graph will be straight line with slope <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>C</mi></mfrac></math>.<br />Slope&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>C</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup></math></p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
